# Does the native commit CLI ignore recorded reds and reject retired red
# admissions, end to end? Its real argument parser and composition require
# the functional route in addition to callable Create tests.
#
# A text carrier is prepared over the original three related/no-path/unreached
# indexes without admission. Both retired keywords must name their body
# replacement. Modified-Go carrier coverage, including the same three indexes
# plus malformed and no-path/unreached controls, is preserved separately in
# TestRunnerGoCreateIgnoresRecordedReds. The real Go composition guard and its
# full-checkout error-inventory floors are unchanged.

option=timeout:value=90s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture runner/commit-not-refused-for-a-red
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=scratch-repo-ready
expect=stdout:contains=owned-red-not-refused
expect=stdout:contains=blind-red-not-refused
expect=stdout:contains=unreached-red-not-refused
expect=stdout:contains=retired-red-admissions-name-the-body
